-- erwartet: C001
-- **664 -- a `section` name that is one blank.**
--
-- The second of `D6`'s assembler-only shapes, and the one that shows why the character set
-- and not the emptiness is the rule. A single space is not an empty name: the C string
-- literal is well formed, `-fsyntax-only` is silent, and the whole of the damage happens
-- when GCC copies the text into a `.section` directive **unquoted**.
--
-- Measured 2026-09-02, before the repair:
--
--     static uint64_t x __attribute__((section(" "))) … = 0;
--     as: Error: missing name
--
-- *The assembler answers the same as it does for the empty name*, which is the giveaway:
-- what it reads is not a name of length one but a directive with nothing on it. Since
-- 2026-09-03 the emitter refuses, and it names the character rather than the length --
-- `` ` ` is not a name character``.
--
-- > **Escaping would not have reached this shape at all.** The candidate repair on the table
-- > for `D6` was to double the backslash, which is a rule about ONE character; a blank has
-- > nothing to escape. *A repair aimed at the shape that was found does not cover the class
-- > it belongs to* -- which is why the refusal is stated as a character set and not as a
-- > list of forbidden characters.

module gift::section_name_that_is_a_space {

static mut x : u64 = 0 section " ";

}
